{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXS72HBdqhFQgksby23p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with a reject. The report's coefficient of 2.07 comes from a regression with no controls, and that is the problem.\n\n- **Replication:** the analyst's code reproduces on the full sample (2.32); on the 1%-trimmed sample the report states 2.066, which I did not re-run on its own. On the full sample, adding the 2020 firm characteristics cuts the estimate to 0.75 (SE 0.23, p = 0.001). On the trimmed sample it is 0.67 (SE 0.22).\n- **Why the estimate shrinks:** remote share is strongly related to pre-period firm size, age and prior patenting, so the unadjusted figure is confounded. Controlling for each of these on its own already pulls the coefficient down: size alone gives 1.25, age 1.93 and prior patenting 2.02.\n- **What survives:** the sign stays positive in every specification I ran. I found no sign of curvature or strong heterogeneity by size or age.\n- **Why reject:** the report ran one specification, with no controls even though the data include pre-period covariates. Its magnitude is about three times too large, so the stated effect size isn't supported.\n\nI did not use `collab_index_2023` as a control in the main comparison. It is measured in 2023, so it may be affected by remote work itself. Adding it flipped the coefficient to about -2.1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":11836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":353,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":452,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d73097-3e62-4f85-a3fd-d7d08b1fe5df","uuid":"664a29b5-921e-4764-a2c4-bf3a5f594274"}
